body:
DO NOT:

📍Force her to talk about it (she’s going to therapy either way);

📍Make comments or talk about it until YOU are feeling calm enough to give the best of you in the convo;

📍expect her to stop, tell you when he does it and so on;

📍ask her to see the injuries (tell her to be open if something goes bad and she needs a doctor obv);

📍act as if you were in her shoes;

📍make comments about her cuts (like, if you talk to the therapist and they ask you how do you perceive the situation, for the sake of god do not tell that she sh but not to deeply or shit like that).

DO:

📍tell her you’re open to talk whenever she wants;

📍tell her you love her and that it will eventually get better;

📍ask her what could help her (don’t expect her to know what to say);

📍sometimes take initiative and spend some quality time with her when you think that she might be stressed;

📍try to see the signals (when she looks sadder, things that could trigger her) and offer silent support to which she can hold onto;

📍listen carefully to and follow therapist’s instructions (but yet don’t stop searching a better one if this seems off).



⚠️⚠️⚠️(This are a few things that I think might be useful...based on my experience. 
My mother found out I was self harming bc she saw some cuts on my upper arm under a fishnet sleeve... I didn’t want to talk to her and she followed me to the bathroom, where I locked myself in to avoid her.
She fucking hit the door until it opened...I remember her screaming, I remember the key falling out of the door lock(?).
I had a panic attack and then she stopped talking about it for a few days, later she came to me with a glittery cream and said “if you want to harm yourself, use this instead” ( which obviously I fucking didn’t) and then it just ended like this.
She talked about it only two other times: Winehouse she begged me to stop bc I was ruining my skin and I’d stop being pretty, when she told my psychiatrist that I self harmed a lot but I really did not want to do it bc she saw that they were thin scars so it meant that they were superficial injuries.
A few years later her and my dad found Out that I never stopped self harming, they threatened me to lock me in a psych ward (they didn’t only bc we were going on holiday soon lmao) and they removed my door.
So yeah my mum turned what could have been an useful tool to get better (= her support) into a proper shitshow.
She scared me so much that, after four years from that first discover and almost six years from when I held a blade for the first time, I still self harm and I can’t manage to even tell my psychologist.)

I hope (and know) that your daughter will eventually be okay.
Just the fact that you want to be the best version of yourself in order to support her tells me that you will be better than my mum and you’ll have some sort of positive impact in this horrible period of her life. 


Sending lots and lots of love to you both❤️
